Receive SMS in ME and periodically recover both memories with bounded polls.

The E1550 SIM answers 6F02 when the modem stores some short last parts of a
long SMS, and the network then retries or drops them. Stored in ME, the modem
itself acknowledges every part to the network.
The init list selects AT+CPMS="ME","ME","ME" (the modem keeps the receive
memory across power cycles; read and write are SM again after ATZ). After
its OK, AT+CPMS="SM" changes only the memory read and deleted, so SMS keep
arriving in ME while the SIM is read in full; then AT+CPMS="ME" and ME is
read in full. If the modem rejects ME, a WARNING is logged, the init list
goes on, and AT+CPMS="SM","SM","SM" keeps SMS enabled on the SIM.
The read memory changes only with no read in flight and no slot waiting;
the FIFO queue sends AT+CPMS after the last CMGR and CMGD of the other
memory. A +CMTI naming the memory being read is read at once. One naming
the other memory ("ME" while the SIM is read, or "SM" for an SMS the modem
still stores on the SIM) never reads or deletes the slot with that number
in the memory being read: that memory is selected for reading when the
inbox is idle, read in full, and reading returns to ME. A memory the modem
rejects for reading is selected again for each later +CMTI that names it.
Any other memory name gets a WARNING without SMS content. Reading still
journals before deletion (ingress patch).
A full read covers slots below the total of the first pair in the
response to the existing AT+CPMS selection, or all 256 slots without valid
counts; used is not a bound, since new SMS take the lowest free slots. The
startup read starts once the selection answers. Empty slots of a full read
are not logged as errors. If a selection of the startup or a periodic pass
is rejected before any memory was read in it, the memory still selected is
read in full once.
600 s (CLOCK_MONOTONIC) after the startup or the previous pass finished,
an idle monitor reads SM, then ME, keeping the receive memory. Channels,
dialing, call waiting, a RING within 60 s, queued commands, reads, slots and
journal retry backoff defer a pass. A pass whose AT+CPMS is not sent ends
with a WARNING; NOTICE logs mark passes with per-memory counts only. A
reconnect replaces the old memory's retry with a fresh read.
Applies after readable-deadline.
